For a response with a content coding, Ladybird reports an unknown length
in every XMLHttpRequest progress event. Chrome 157 does the same,
verified at runtime: Its URLRequestJob takes the expected content size
from Content-Length only when no decoding SourceStream filters the body,
so XMLHttpRequest::DispatchProgressEvent() gets no length.

WebKit, in XMLHttpRequest::didReceiveData(), reports Content-Length as
the total until the received length passes it, which for a small gzipped
body happens at the first event (verified at runtime in Playwright’s
WebKit 26.5). Firefox 151 reports the encoded bytes received against
Content-Length instead, so its events stay length-computable.
